From b3c46877bfafec617265d5540b46a6bd0fada1cd Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Tue, 29 Sep 2026 04:56:17 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/3] QR & Barcode Scanner: read the codes Morpho could only
 write

Morpho generated QR codes and barcodes and could not read one, which is
half a tool - the person who makes a code is usually the one who later
needs to check what is actually on it. It sits in the Generator category
beside the two writers, which is where someone looking for it will go.

Decoding is deliberately stubborn. One pass with the default binarizer
misses a lot of real pictures: photos of screens, printed labels under
uneven light, codes shot at an angle. Two binarizers across four
rotations is still well under a second on a 1600px bitmap and turns most
of those misses into reads. The multiple reader runs first, because a
photo of a sheet of labels holds more than one code and returning only
the first is wrong.

The bitmap is capped at 1600px before decoding: RGBLuminanceSource needs
the pixels as an IntArray, four bytes each, so a full 12MP photo would
allocate 48MB to read a code that needs none of that resolution.

Each result says what the payload is - Wi-Fi network, contact card,
web link, product number - before the user acts on it, rather than
handing back a raw string. A miss says what to change about the photo
instead of just failing.

Two generic icon keys added (camera, scan) rather than borrowing another
tool's id as an icon key. No file under ads/ is touched.

