From 29ec590361105f167ac4c4af7e43eade12546044 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Tue, 29 Sep 2026 04:59:11 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2/3] Passport & ID Photo: exact sizes, ready to print

An ID photo is a physical measurement, not a pixel count, so the tool
works in millimetres and dpi: pick 35 x 45 mm at 300 dpi and you get
413 x 531 px, which is what a print shop needs. Five common formats,
300 or 600 dpi, and an optional 6 x 4 in sheet tiled with copies and
hairline cut guides, which is how these are actually printed.

Background replacement reuses the ML Kit subject segmentation already in
the build for Background Remover, so a plain backdrop costs no new
dependency and no upload.

Two deliberate honesty calls. Sizes are named by their millimetres with a
note on the format, never as a claim about any authority's current rules
- those vary by document and change, and the pitch says to check the form.
And there is no face detector in this app's dependencies, so the crop is
manual: a vertical offset the user sets against a live preview, labelled
as theirs to set. Implying an alignment the app cannot perform would be
the kind of promise that earns the review we are digging out of.

135 tools, every one dispatched and every one with a pitch. No file under
ads/ is touched.

